<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>BACKUP 1 · CONSTRUCT VALIDITY</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        What each arm actually sees
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 14, lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
        One source string, three encoders. None of them is handed a chain-level field.
    </Text>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 18, marginTop: 18 }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 240, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '14px 16px', background: '#16233A', border: '1px solid #2F4A75', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#4D8DFF', letterSpacing: 1, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>INPUT</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#FFFFFF', marginTop: 4, lineHeight: 1.3 }}>one PSMILES string per repeat unit</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#93A8C2', marginTop: 6, lineHeight: 1.35 }}>18,152 structures · one string each</Text>
        </Box>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, color: '#5A7192', width: 24, textAlign: 'center' }}>→</Text>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 10 }}>
            {[
                ['A2 · descriptors', '205 RDKit descriptors + 2048-bit Morgan fingerprint → XGBoost', '#C3D0E2'],
                ['A3 · graph', 'atoms and bonds of the same string → chemprop MPNN', '#4D8DFF'],
                ['A4 · language model', 'the same string, tokenised → frozen polyBERT → ridge head', '#4D8DFF'],
            ].map(([head, body, color]) => (
                <Box key={head} style={{ flexDirection: 'column', padding: '10px 14px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 5 }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, fontWeight: 'bold', color: color }}>{head}</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 2, lineHeight: 1.35 }}>{body}</Text>
                </Box>
            ))}
        </Box>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, color: '#5A7192', width: 24, textAlign: 'center' }}>→</Text>
        <Box style={{ width: 190, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '14px 16px', background: '#16233A', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#93A8C2', letterSpacing: 1, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>TARGET</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#FFFFFF', marginTop: 4, lineHeight: 1.3 }}>the same measured property for all three</Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', padding: '14px 20px', background: '#111B2E', borderLeft: '3px solid #FFB020' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, color: '#FFB020', fontWeight: 'bold', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
            So &quot;chain-aware&quot; here means a richer encoding of the same repeat unit — not extra chain information.
        </Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 6, lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
            Molar-mass distribution, sequence, tacticity, morphology and processing history are absent from every arm, because the release does not carry them.
            That is a limit on what claim 01 can mean, and it is why we say &quot;chain-aware arms&quot; rather than &quot;chain information&quot;.
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 12 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>Backup · not presented</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>B1</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
